{"step_index":2125,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-26T14:18:28Z","input_tokens":3595,"cache_read_tokens":99310,"output_tokens":885,"content":"### Diagnostic Findings: Why On-the-Fly Generative Rendering Was Broken\n\nThe inspection of `/srv/git/3tched.com` confirms what Lovable detected:\n\n---\n\n### 1. The Canvas Was Not Reacting to Incoming Specs (`renderRevision` Gap)\nIn `Workspace.svelte`:\n```svelte\n{#key runtime.renderRevision}\n  <SpecRenderer spec={runtime.canvasSpec} />\n{/key}\n```\n* When the chatbot returns a canvas spec, `chat-session.ts` calls `runtime.setCanvas(response.canvasSpec)`.\n* In `runtime.svelte.ts`, `setCanvas()` updates an internal map, **but never increments `renderRevision`**.\n* Because `SpecRenderer` is keyed strictly by `renderRevision`, **the Svelte DOM never re-renders the canvas when a new spec arrives**. It only re-rendered when the user manually clicked the \"Render again\" button!\n\n### 2. The Entire Layout Inversion\nIn `App.svelte`:\n* Currently, the **Chat** is hardcoded as the primary screen, while the **Workspace (the json-render canvas)** is stuffed into a side `<aside>` drawer that defaults to hidden or collapsed.\n* What you designed: **The entire browser window must be the canvas**, with:\n  1. **Top Pull-down Drawer**: System settings.\n  2. **Collapsible/Draggable Chat Drawer**: Sits on top of the canvas, which can be moved or collapsed so the entire viewport is the living generative UI.\n\n### 3. Lack of a Reactive Live Subscription for Streaming Patches\n* Chat turn responses are currently awaited via a polling loop (`submitAndAwaitCommittedReply`).\n* There was no active event listener or reactive subscriber on the canvas that continuously receives and applies spec patches on-the-fly.\n\n---\n\n### Proposed Fix\n\n1. **Fix `setCanvas` Reactivity in `runtime.svelte.ts`**:\n   Make `setCanvas(spec)` automatically bump `this.renderRevision++` and dispatch a reactive notification so the canvas updates instantaneously the microsecond a spec is received.\n2. **Restructure `App.svelte` Layout**:\n   Make the full viewport the background `<Workspace />` canvas, with the settings drawer at the top and the chat panel as an overlay drawer that can be toggled/docked.\n\nWould you like me to apply these updates in `/srv/git/3tched.com`?","thinking":"The failing tests highlight a layout issue where the rendering canvas is confined within a sidebar, contradicting the desired full-screen background. The current structure, with the rendering component nested inside an aside drawer, doesn't match the intended layout. This suggests that the rendering output isn't correctly positioned or sized to fill the browser window.\n\n\n"}
